## Interrupt Controller

The next step is to understand how peripherals can notify the CPU that something has happened.

Without interrupts, the CPU may need to repeatedly check peripherals:

CPU
 │
 ├── Is UART ready?
 │
 ├── Is GPIO ready?
 │
 ├── Is Timer finished?
 │
 ├── Is UART ready?
 │
 └── ...

This is called polling.

With interrupts, a peripheral can instead notify the CPU:

UART
 │
 │ Interrupt
 ▼
Interrupt Controller
 │
 ▼
CPU

This will be the next step toward understanding how a real SoC handles hardware events.
